# Aircover API credentials.
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values, OR pass these on the
# command line. .env is in .gitignore and will not be committed.

# ─── Option A: Username + password ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Works for accounts that can log in via Aircover's /auth/login endpoint.
AIRCOVER_USERNAME=your-username@your-company.com
AIRCOVER_PASSWORD=your-password

# ─── Option B: Bearer token (for SSO-only accounts) ────────────────────────
# Use these instead of USERNAME/PASSWORD when your account logs in via SSO
# and can't use /auth/login.
#
# How to get the tokens:
#   1. Open app.aircover.ai and log in via SSO.
#   2. Open browser dev tools (F12 or Cmd+Opt+I).
#   3. Go to: Application -> Local Storage -> https://app.aircover.ai
#   4. Find a key containing "authInfo" (or the access_token/refresh_token
#      values directly). It's a JSON blob with `access_token` and
#      `refresh_token` fields.
#   5. Copy each value (the long string starting with "eyJ...") below.
#
# The refresh token typically lives ~60 days. The access token lives ~1
# hour but is auto-refreshed by the script as long as the refresh token
# is set. Without a refresh token, the script can still run but will start
# failing once the access token expires.
#
# AIRCOVER_ACCESS_TOKEN=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
# AIRCOVER_REFRESH_TOKEN=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

# ─── Option C: API token ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Static API key (starts with "ac_"). Requires AIRCOVER_CUSTOMER_ORG.
# No login or token refresh needed.
# AIRCOVER_API_TOKEN=ac_your_api_token_here
# AIRCOVER_CUSTOMER_ORG=postman.com

# ─── Optional: Customer org (for Options A & B) ───────────────────────────
# Sent as the X-Aircover-Org header on every API request. Required for
# Option C (API token); optional for Options A & B.
# AIRCOVER_CUSTOMER_ORG=postman.com
